---
3md: 1.0
axis: skill
agent: web-tester
tools: sh, screencapture
persona: drives real Google Chrome via System Events UI-scripting and captures a real screenshot, no headless browser
---
Test agent for the Web target. Uses Google Chrome (already installed, no
Playwright/Chromium download needed) as the driver, automated through
AppleScript — the same Accessibility bridge the macOS target uses for native
apps. Chrome, not Safari, deliberately: this drives a real GUI browser
window, and Chrome isn't the daily-driver browser on the machines this
gets developed/tested on.

@plane z=0 label="web-tester" kind=identity
# web-tester

Open the page, read back its title as the cheapest possible assertion, then
capture a screenshot artifact.

@plane z=1 label="open" kind=skill triggers="web, page, url, browser, navigate, load" inputs="url:string" tool="sh scripts/web-open.sh {url}"
# Skill: open

Open {url} in Google Chrome via System Events keystrokes (not Chrome's own
Apple Events dictionary — see scripts/web-open.sh for why) and return the
resulting front window's name. Assert it is non-empty.

@plane z=2 label="screenshot" kind=skill triggers="screenshot, snapshot, capture, image" inputs="path:string" tool="screencapture -x {path}" cost="fs"
# Skill: screenshot

Full-screen capture to {path}, no shutter sound (`-x`). Run after [[z=1|open]]
so the captured frame shows the loaded page.
